 States</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/94888856-c05a-4378-833d-59c265df698b.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/1941\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Remand\nNormally a\nJenks Act [underlined: statement]\nis one signed or\nacknowledged by\nwitness.\n( I believe Byron\nagree with me that\nthese notes are\nnot &quot;statements&quot; )\n\nRemand\n\nBlackmun, J. [underlined: Remand]\nFact that atty is\nauthor is not\ncontrolling\nNothing to Brady\npoint\n\nPowell, J. [inserted: Remand as to 40 Pages] [struck: [illegible]] Affirm\non merits\n1. Newman&#x27;s 40 pages, I\ncould remand for consideration\nof these [underlined: in camera] by DC to\ndetermine whether they requir\na retrial (unlikely from what\nwas said about contents); or I\ncould [struck: I] ignore as not within\n[struck: Cert] Grant of Cert. Petr. made\nno effort to enlarge Grant.\n2. Merits. Affirm.\n[underlined: Jenks Act] §(e)(1) applies\nonly [struck: to] to a statement &quot;made&quot; &amp;\n&quot;signed or otherwise adopted or\napproved&quot; by witness.\nNot clear from this record\nthat Witness Newman &quot;adopted&quot;\nor &quot;approved&quot; anything. At most,\nhis approval was [inserted: too] fragmentary\nto constitute a statement.\nCampbell II involved a coherent\nstatement &amp; can be distinguished\n(It is an unsound opinion.)\n\nRehnquist, J. [underlined: Affirm on Merits]\n( agree on\n\nPowell (cont)\nBrady issue: Not dispositive,\nas no showing that\nany of notes were\nexculpatory. Extremely\nunlikely that they would\nhave been.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div 